**Give the worker bounded time before suspension.**

The `Suspending` handler writes `.cancel` and returns without obtaining a deferral. The OS can suspend the app before `run_job` consumes the marker. This can repeat up to 63 trunk steps. During cooldown, the branch artifact may not be written, so an explicit resume must repeat that cooldown. The work is recoverable, but the training workflow is delayed.

Obtain a deferral and complete it from a bounded waiter. Use `active_changed` to detect worker completion. `wait_for` releases `active_mutex` while it waits, and the waiter keeps the UI handler from blocking.

<details>
<summary>Suggested suspension handling</summary>

```diff
 #include <chrono>
+#include <condition_variable>
 #include <filesystem>
@@
 std::mutex active_mutex;
 std::filesystem::path active_job;
+std::condition_variable active_changed;
@@
         {
           std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(active_mutex);
           active_job.clear();
         }
+        active_changed.notify_all();
@@
-  Suspending([](auto const &, auto const &) {
-    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(active_mutex);
-    if (!active_job.empty()) {
-      std::ofstream file(active_job.parent_path() /
-                         (active_job.stem().stem().wstring() + L".cancel"));
-      file << "suspend";
+  Suspending([](auto const &, auto const &args) {
+    auto deferral = args.SuspendingOperation().GetDeferral();
+    {
+      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(active_mutex);
+      if (!active_job.empty()) {
+        std::ofstream file(active_job.parent_path() /
+                           (active_job.stem().stem().wstring() + L".cancel"));
+        file << "suspend";
+      }
     }
+    std::thread([deferral]() mutable {
+      std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lock(active_mutex);
+      active_changed.wait_for(lock, std::chrono::seconds(4),
+                              [] { return active_job.empty(); });
+      lock.unlock();
+      deferral.Complete();
+    }).detach();
   });
```

